20.Email Body Analysis & Attachment Analysis
After analyzing the email header, the next step is to focus on the email body. This is often where the true intention of a phishing email is revealed.
The email body is usually where attackers deliver their malicious payload through:
•	Malicious hyperlinks 
•	Fake login pages 
•	Dangerous attachments 
•	Embedded scripts or content 
During analysis, links should be extracted from:
•	Visible email content 
•	HTML source code 
•	Raw email message source 
This helps identify hidden or obfuscated URLs.
________________________________________
Mail Body Analysis
Link Investigation
A simple way to investigate a link inside an email is:
1.	Right-click the link. 
2.	Select: 
Copy Link Address
(The option name may vary depending on the email client or browser.)
3.	Analyze the URL without opening it. 
This allows analysts to determine:
•	The real destination. 
•	Whether the domain is suspicious. 
•	Whether the link contains redirects. 
________________________________________
