Email Attachments
Attachments are one of the most common methods attackers use to deliver malware.
Examples:
•	PDF files 
•	Microsoft Office documents 
•	Executable files 
•	Archive files 
A suspicious attachment should never be opened directly.
________________________________________
Safe Attachment Handling
Attachments should only be downloaded and analyzed in a controlled environment:
Examples:
•	Virtual machine (VM) 
•	Sandbox 
•	Malware analysis lab 
Purpose:
•	Prevent accidental execution. 
•	Protect the analyst's system. 
________________________________________
SHA256 Hash Analysis
After safely obtaining an attachment, analysts should generate a hash value.
A hash provides a unique identifier for the file and can be used for threat intelligence searches.
Example command:
sha256sum shady_attachment.pdf
Example output:
025ba9ce4a2118a9ca7b115c8869ff73bc16bad3732ba359cef1e60ad8f961f9 shady_attachment.pdf
The SHA256 hash can be searched in security databases to determine whether the file is known to be malicious.
