21.Malware Sandbox Analysis
Defenders do not always need advanced malware reverse engineering skills to understand malicious attachments.
Instead, they can use malware sandboxes.
A malware sandbox is a controlled environment where suspicious files can be safely executed and analyzed without risking the analyst’s own system.
